WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.900
Dear Fellow Scholars, this is Two Minute Papers
with Károly Zsolnai-Fehér.

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:09.410
We already know that by using a computer,
we can simulate fluids and we can simulate

00:00:09.410 --> 00:00:10.410
hair.

00:00:10.410 --> 00:00:13.959
But what about simulating both of them at
the same time?

00:00:13.959 --> 00:00:19.470
This paper is about liquid-hair interaction
and simulating the dynamics of wet hair.

00:00:19.470 --> 00:00:24.710
Our seasoned Fellow Scholars immediately know
that this episode is going to be ample in

00:00:24.710 --> 00:00:26.539
amazing slow motion footage.

00:00:26.539 --> 00:00:31.730
I hope I didn't mess up with any of them,
you will see soon if this is the case or not!

00:00:31.730 --> 00:00:36.350
Before we start talking about it, I'd like
to note the following remarkable features:

00:00:36.350 --> 00:00:42.350
the authors uploaded a supplementary video
in 4k resolution, executable files for their

00:00:42.350 --> 00:00:48.379
technique for all 3 major operating systems,
data assets, and they also freshly revealed

00:00:48.379 --> 00:00:50.360
the full source code of the project.

00:00:50.360 --> 00:00:51.450
Hell yeah!

00:00:51.450 --> 00:00:53.270
I feel in heaven.

00:00:53.270 --> 00:00:58.790
A big, Two Minute Papers style hat tip to
the authors for this premium quality presentation.

00:00:58.790 --> 00:01:03.530
If this paper were a car, it would definitely
be a Maserati or a Mercedes.

00:01:03.530 --> 00:01:09.440
This technique solves the equations for liquid
motion along every single hair strand, computes

00:01:09.440 --> 00:01:14.920
the cohesion effects between the hairs, and
it can also simulate the effect of water dripping

00:01:14.920 --> 00:01:16.200
off the hair.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:20.000
Feast your eyes on these absolutely incredible
results.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:25.330
The main issue with such an idea is that the
theory of large, and small-scale simulations

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:28.950
are inherently different, and in this case,
we need both.

00:01:28.950 --> 00:01:34.340
The large-scale simulator would be a standard
program that is able to compute how the velocity

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:36.920
and pressure of the liquid evolves in time.

00:01:36.920 --> 00:01:42.460
However, we also wish to model the water droplets
contained within one tiny hair strand.

00:01:42.460 --> 00:01:48.290
With a large-scale simulator, this would take
a stupendously large amount of time and resources,

00:01:48.290 --> 00:01:53.450
so the key observation is that a small-scale
fluid simulator program would be introduced

00:01:53.450 --> 00:01:54.850
take care of this.

00:01:54.850 --> 00:02:00.100
However, these two simulators cannot simply
coexist without side effects.

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.890
As they are two separate programs that work
on the very same scene, we have to make sure

00:02:04.890 --> 00:02:09.930
that as we pass different quantities between
them, they will still remain intact.

00:02:09.930 --> 00:02:14.390
This means that a drop of water that gets
trapped in a hair strand has to disappear

00:02:14.390 --> 00:02:19.070
from the large-scale simulator, and has to
be readded to it when it drips out.

00:02:19.070 --> 00:02:21.340
This is a remarkably challenging problem.

00:02:21.340 --> 00:02:24.110
But with this, we only scratched the surface.

00:02:24.110 --> 00:02:28.530
Make sure to have a look at the paper that
has so much more to offer, it is impossible

00:02:28.530 --> 00:02:32.840
to even enumerate the list of contributions
within in such a short video.

00:02:32.840 --> 00:02:38.000
The quality of this paper simply left me speechless
and I would encourage you to take a look as

00:02:38.000 --> 00:02:39.000
well.

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:42.560
And while this amazing footage is rolling,
I would like to let you know that Two Minute

00:02:42.560 --> 00:02:46.520
Papers can exist because of your support through
Patreon.

00:02:46.520 --> 00:02:51.170
Supporters of the series gain really cool
perks like watching every single one of these

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:52.950
episodes in early access.

00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:58.290
I am super happy to see how many of you decided
